{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they hammered out.</b> Like ״לְרֹקַע הָאָרֶץ״ (Psalms 136); as its Targum renders וּרְדִידוּ — they would hammer out plates from the gold, אשטנ״דרא בְּלַעַז, thin plates. Here it teaches you how they would spin the gold with the threads: they hammer thin plates, and cut from them lengthwise strips — to make them threads, a mixture with each and every kind in the breastplate and ephod in which gold was used: one thread of gold with six threads of tekhelet, and likewise with each and every kind — for all the kinds are a thread folded sixfold, and the gold is the seventh thread with each and every one."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French estendre, 'to stretch/hammer out'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:52.959944977Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}